But based on press accounts, we think that it's possible that they serve 10,000 people but seat only 4,000 at a time.

00:43:59.120 --> 00:44:00.860
Foxconn wouldn't answer the question for us directly.

00:44:02.260 --> 00:44:07.040
When it comes to the suicide rate at Foxconn, there were about 12 suicides at the Shenzhen plant in 2010.

00:44:07.500 --> 00:44:09.260
It's actually hard to get the exact number.

00:44:10.000 --> 00:44:18.060
Some people have pointed out that 12 suicides for 400,000 workers is actually much lower than China's suicide rate as a whole.

00:44:18.240 --> 00:44:23.380
China has an unusually high suicide rate of 22 suicides per year per 100,000 people.

00:44:24.160 --> 00:44:27.520
That would work out to 88 suicides for 400,000 workers.

00:44:28.440 --> 00:44:32.440
Mike Daisy points out that we don't actually know if these are the only suicides at Foxconn.

00:44:33.420 --> 00:44:38.840
And the biggest problem is that it isn't the quantity, it's the cluster.

00:44:38.840 --> 00:44:54.500
You know, if there was any company in America where a sizable chunk of your workforce went up over a period of time, especially close to one another, and killed themselves in the same way very publicly, it would be an enormous news story because it's far outside the norm.

00:44:55.040 --> 00:44:57.260
Overall, we checked with over a dozen people.

00:44:57.860 --> 00:45:07.960
There would be journalists who cover these factories, people who work with the electronics industry in China, activists, labor groups, about the working conditions that Mike Daisy describes in his show.

00:45:08.640 --> 00:45:10.160
And nobody seemed very surprised by them.

00:45:10.420 --> 00:45:16.040
Well, unfortunately, I think some of these conditions sound actually quite common.

