This is Ian Spalding, who estimates that he has been in or worked with about 1,000 factories throughout China.

00:45:22.050 --> 00:45:31.750
The company that he founded and runs, In Fact Global Partners, goes into Chinese factories and helps them meet social responsibility standards that are set by Western companies.

00:45:32.000 --> 00:45:36.100
So those companies are ready when outside auditors come and check on working conditions.

00:45:36.820 --> 00:45:40.320
He has a staff of 45 that do hundreds of factories a year, including electronics.

00:45:41.040 --> 00:45:46.940
There are hours in factories that are often too long and are excessive and required over time.

00:45:47.120 --> 00:45:47.280
time.

00:45:47.800 --> 00:45:55.500
Things like cramped quarters can also happen, and repetitive motion injuries are also can be quite common.

00:45:56.500 --> 00:46:02.960
Another thing that Mike Daisy says that's disturbing to hear is he says that the companies will deceive the auditors when the auditors come in.

00:46:03.660 --> 00:46:04.180
Have you seen that?

00:46:04.600 --> 00:46:09.700
Yeah, that actually is quite common, and I think many other people have also exposed this problem.

00:46:10.560 --> 00:46:11.400
Now, don't get the wrong impression.

